main-flight-opt.py
Runnable example using Mealpy to solve a relevant airline problem: Dynamic 3D Flight 
Trajectory Optimization through a changing wind and weather vector field.This model 
optimizes a flight's vertical profile (altitude changes) and speed strategy over a 
series of checkpoints to minimize total operating costs (combining fuel burn, carbon 
taxes, and delay penalties) while actively avoiding severe convective weather (turbulence/storms).

multi-pareto-flight.py:
Multi-Objective Optimization (MOO) framework, we stop combining Fuel and Time 
into a single cash value. Instead, we treat them as conflicting objectives to 
find the Pareto Front—the set of optimal flight paths where you cannot improve flight 
time without burning more fuel (and vice versa). While Mealpy is excellent for 
single-objective problems, DEAP is the industry standard in Python for handling 
true Pareto multi-objective optimization using NSGA-II (Non-dominated Sorting Genetic Algorithm II).